---
/**
 * Leagues — the retention engine, and the worst-executed page type in the
 * corpus. Ported to the converged Paper design 2026-08-03 (FW-3967);
 * spec in `design/SUBPAGE-EXPLORATION.md`.
 *
 * **The idea: the season is a TRACK, not a catalogue.** The track was written in
 * August, when both venues were between seasons and a page built as a list of
 * leagues you could join would have been a page whose every row said "no". It
 * earns its place just as much now that registration is open: the question has
 * moved from "is there anything?" to "when does it start and how long is it",
 * and the track answers that in the same three cells. That is why `SeasonTrack`
 * sits in the hero-strip position: it is the ONE justified exception to the
 * 4-cell strip, same furniture, but its rule is only partly filled because
 * progress is the fact it exists to show.
 *
 * ⚠️ The track's three steps are HARDCODED here and its `activeIndex` with them.
 * They are the one part of this page that does not follow the collection, so a
 * season change has to move them by hand — they said "there is nothing to
 * register for yet" for a fortnight after registration opened if nobody did.
 * Check them whenever `state` changes on a live row.
 *
 * **The capture band is the largest thing after the hero**, deliberately. Across
 * all 126 audited simulator and golf-course sites, exactly ZERO offered a
 * waitlist, while 11% of league pages say "registration closed" and simply stop
 * (playbook-core.md §5). The one component nobody else has should not be a
 * footnote. (126 is the WHOLE audit — sim venues plus golf courses; the 96 in
 * `data/global.ts` is the sim-venue subset. Always name which. And keep the
 * comparison internal: it is a competitive claim about named third parties and
 * belongs in comments, never in copy a customer reads.)
 *
 * **The band is also this page's one ember field.** SUBPAGE-EXPLORATION §"Paper
 * quirks" flags that ember goes unused on dark-heavy pages, because every CTA on
 * a dark block inverts to an amber fill. A page that never shows the brand's
 * action colour is worth avoiding, so the capture band is ember at full strength
 * — once, like the homepage's.
 *
 * **"On the blanks" is the page's closing note and it is a promise, not an
 * apology.** The note commits to publishing night, format, length and price
 * TOGETHER, before registration opens rather than after you have paid. Nobody
 * asked for that. The 2026 fall lineup is the first time that promise has come
 * due, and it was kept: all four are on every Lakeville block, published the day
 * registration opened rather than after. Keep it that way — the note is now a
 * claim with a precedent behind it, which is worth more than the claim was.
 *
 * ── THE 2026 FALL SEASON LANDED 2026-09-04 ─────────────────────────────────
 *
 * CJ supplied the fall lineup and it changed what this page is. Five rows are
 * `state: 'open'` with real register links — four Lakeville nights and, for the
 * first time, Stillwater. Registration is at two different providers, which is
 * why the link lives per-league on the collection rather than once on the page.
 *
 * The nine blocks that follow the collection needed no code: `status: 'archive'`
 * still draws Lakeville's four older seasons disabled and they now sort BELOW
 * the live rows (`order` 6–9), so the first thing on the page is something you
 * can act on. That is the collection doing the job it exists to do.
 *
 * **The entry fee is no longer a blanket gap, and the distinction still matters.**
 * Lakeville's fall rows carry a real `price` — $700 per team, from CJ's own
 * lineup document — and that is an ENTRY FEE, unlike the dollar figures on the
 * archived sheets, which are SKINS BUY-INS ("to be paid at beginning of the
 * season"). The two fields stay separate for exactly that reason; see
 * `LeagueBlock`'s facts table. Stillwater's document states no price at all, so
 * its Cost cell is still a gap and must stay one until CJ supplies the figure.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeagueBlock from '../components/venue/LeagueBlock.astro';
import LeagueSchema from '../components/venue/LeagueSchema.astro';
import SeasonTrack from '../components/venue/SeasonTrack.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/venue/SectionHead.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/venue/WaitlistForm.astro';
import { LEAGUE_WAITLIST_ID, upcomingSeason } from '../lib/leagues';

const leagues = (await getCollection('leagues'))
  .filter((l) => l.data.published)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);

/**
 * Named from the first row that is NOT archived — see `upcomingSeason`.
 * Lakeville's archived seasons sort first because they are the rows with facts
 * in them, and reading `leagues[0]` here would have the capture band offering
 * first word on a season that finished last December.
 */
const season = upcomingSeason(leagues);

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'Indoor Golf Leagues — Lakeville & Stillwater, MN',
  metaDescription:
    'Register for 2026 fall simulator golf leagues at The Links, Lakeville and Stillwater MN. Two-person teams, handicapped and beginner-friendly. Play starts the week of 4 October.',
};

/**
 * The three steps of a season, in order over time — the site's ONE sanctioned
 * use of the `01 / 02 / 03` numerals after convergence. `activeIndex` is 0
 * because both venues are between seasons today; move it when the lineup lands
 * and the filled rule moves with it.
 */
const steps = [
  {
    marker: 'Now',
    title: 'Registration is open',
    body: 'Both venues are taking teams for the fall season. Pick your night and sign up — teams fill fastest in the first week.',
  },
  {
    marker: 'Next',
    title: 'Play starts the week of 4 October',
    body: 'You play the same night every week: Monday to Thursday at Lakeville, Sunday to Thursday at Stillwater.',
  },
  {
    marker: 'Then',
    title: 'Ten weeks, through mid-December',
    body: 'Lakeville runs eight weeks of regular season and two of playoffs, with Thanksgiving week off.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {
    /* 1. HERO — midnight, venue-neutral. The season is named in the eyebrow
      because "which season is this page about" is the first question a returning
      player has, and half the corpus never answers it. */
  }
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter pt-s8 pb-s7 lg:px-gutter-lg lg:pt-s9 lg:pb-s8">
      <p class="caps-label text-amber">{season}</p>
      <h1 class="mt-s5 text-hero leading-hero font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-white">Leagues</h1>
      <p class="mt-s5 max-w-prose-page border-l-slab border-amber pl-s4 text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        The cheapest way to play all winter, and the fastest way to meet people who also think Tuesday is a golf night.
        Handicaps keep matches fair, so a first-timer and a scratch player can be on the same team.
      </p>

      {
        /* 2. THE SEASON TRACK, in the hero-strip position. The justified
          exception — see the file header and `SeasonTrack`. */
      }
      <SeasonTrack class="mt-s8" steps={steps} activeIndex={0} tone="dark" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* 3. THE CAPTURE BAND. The largest thing after the hero, and the page's one
      ember field at full strength.

      Nothing dark goes on this band: midnight on ember is 2.35:1 and navy
      1.79:1 — the same measurement that forbids an ember fill on the hero, read
      the other way round. The form therefore sits in a paper slab punched out of
      the band, and inside that slab everything reverts to light-field styling. */
  }
  <section class="on-accent-band bg-primary" id={LEAGUE_WAITLIST_ID}>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <div class="grid gap-s7 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-start lg:gap-s9">
        <div>
          <p class="caps-label text-white">Open now</p>
          <h2 class="mt-s4 text-section leading-display font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-white">
            Registration is open for {season}
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-s5 text-lead leading-body text-surface">
            Both venues are taking teams. Every league below has its own sign-up link — Lakeville and Stillwater
            register in different places, so use the button on the night you want.
          </p>
          <p
            class="my-s6 border-y-score border-white py-s4 font-display text-row leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-white"
          >
            Teams fill fastest in the first week.
          </p>
        </div>

        {
          /* The list survives an open season, and this is the state it was built
            for as much as the empty one. A night that fills, or four nights that
            all fall wrong, is exactly where 11% of the corpus says "registration
            closed" and stops. Here it still ends somewhere. */
        }
        <WaitlistForm
          listName="league-general"
          heading="Can't make these nights?"
          blurb="If a night fills or these dates do not suit, one email when the next season opens. Nothing else, ever."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 4. THE VENUE BLOCKS — one ruled column, not two cards. */}
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={1}>League play at both venues</SectionHead>
      {leagues.map((league, i) => <LeagueBlock league={league} first={i === 0} last={i === leagues.length - 1} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* 5. ON THE BLANKS. The closing note, and a commitment rather than a
      disclaimer. It is on greige so it reads as the page's own aside — and note
      that emberMid is 3.66:1 on greige (`rules.noWarningOnGreige`), which is why
      nothing here is set in the caution colour. */
  }
  <section class="bg-greige">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={2}>On the blanks</SectionHead>
      <div class="max-w-prose-page">
        <p class="text-lead leading-body text-inkBody">
          Most of the season above is filled in, and that is new. Every Lakeville night now states what it costs to
          enter, not just what the skins pot is — the two are different numbers and this page will never quietly use one
          for the other. Two things are still blank and are marked rather than guessed: Stillwater's lineup arrived with
          its nights and format but no price, and prizes are not set at either venue. Lakeville's older seasons are kept
          at the bottom as reference, not registration.
        </p>
        <p
          class="mt-s5 border-l-slab border-ember pl-s4 font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink"
        >
          We said we would publish night, format, length and price together, before registration opened rather than
          after you had paid. That is what the Lakeville blocks above are.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-s5 text-body leading-body text-inkBody">
          If a league night has to change once it is running, everyone playing hears it from us first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <LeagueSchema leagues={leagues} />
</BaseLayout>
